    "narrative": "For the 2026-06-12 slate, **Josh Naylor** (77.77) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) headline our offensive output. Both benefit significantly from facing favorable starting pitching in Littell (4.78 xERA) and Imai (4.75 xERA), respectively. **Josh Naylor** finds himself in a prime spot as the cleanup anchor, buoyed by a 19% boost from the opposing SP skill set and a favorable platoon advantage. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** is poised for production at 1B, leveraging a 14% boost from his dynamic platoon splits against Imai. **Corbin Carroll** remains an elite start (71.85) despite the matchup against Lodolo; while the dynamic platoon split is a slight drag, his raw upside and speed profile\u2014critical for our scarcity-driven strategy\u2014keep him locked in as a primary engine for our Runs and SB categories.\n\nThe benching of **Austin Riley** (44.03) represents the most difficult cut of the day. Despite a solid base projection, he is penalized heavily by the 3.33 xERA of McLean and a park factor that suppresses his ceiling compared to the likes of **Kyle Karros** (59.95), who earns the start at 3B largely due to a superior matchup against the 4.48 xERA of Jump. We are also keeping a close watch on **Brice Turang** (49.77); while his score is marginal, his utility in the SB department forces our hand, even as we account for the negative impact of his facing a sub-4.00 xERA arm in Banks. We continue to monitor the status of **Mickey Moniak**, who remains on the IL; his absence necessitates disciplined management of our active depth, though we are confident the remaining lineup carries enough efficiency to sustain our current Roto trajectory.",
